5. Conditional constructive opening: separate stress distribution, crack resistance and chemical renewal

ROOT's own script explicitly introduces100 scalar patches with15N capacity and40um total height scatter. At1000N total and common displacement, k=1MN/m perpatch overloads the highest patch at28.2251N, while many others are lightly loaded. Softening to100kN/m distributes8--12N but increases displacement to.1mm. An introduced12N force plateau with1MN/m initial slope caps every live patch at12N; with10dead patches the remaining90 still support1000N at24.1616um displacement. This is a positive static load-sharing construction within its one-dimensional force law. No manufacturable spring, moment capacity, lateral constraint, crack-arrest network or adhesive qualification is supplied. The read dry-gripper architecture already establishes the general load-sharing principle.

For the source lap-compliance relation, separately INTRODUCED A=.0025m2,G_on=2J/m2,G_off=.02J/m2,C_hold=1e-8m/N,C_release=1e-5m/N give1000N on/stiff,100N off/stiff,31.6228N on/soft and3.16228N off/soft. Thus an introduced100-fold fracture-energy change gives only tenfold force change at fixed compliance; a separately constructed geometry change could supply additional release leverage. The off energy and switchable support are NOT measured source properties. This calculation is not a new adhesive or free way to switch compliance under a load.

A second independent screen derives a clamped circular thin-plate blister under fixed uniform pressure:
D=E*h^3/[12*(1-nu^2)];
w(r)=p*(a^2-r^2)^2/(64D);
V=pi*p*a^6/(192D);
G=p^2*a^4/(128D).
For introduced p=200kPa and INTRODUCED mode-I G=2J/m2, a1mm backing with introducedE70GPa,nu.3 gives critical radius14.2319mm; a132um film with introducedE3GPa,nu.38 gives1.44010mm. Only the132um thickness was actually read in the PFSA specimen. Its lap-derived2.02J/m2 is NOT supplied mode-I toughness. Actual edge/mixed-mode cracks, shear transfer, residual stresses, plasticity, film thickness and load-control conditions remain essential. These two geometries show why a high lap strength cannot be transplanted into a thin normal-load pad, and why stiff supported contact cells deserve investigation rather than being assumed to work.

